{"tool_name":"deepcell","contents":["neubias","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"deepcell","home":"https://www.deepcell.org","summary":"Accurate cell tracking and lineage construction in live-cell imaging experiments with deep learning.\n\nHome \u2014 DeepCell 1.0.0 documentation.\n\nFree document hosting provided by Read the Docs","addition_date":"2020-01-09T18:27:38Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:38:22.175336Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:deepcell","documentation":[{"type":["FAQ"],"url":"https://www.deepcell.org/faq"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www.deepcell.org/about"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://deepcell.readthedocs.io/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"},{"term":"Image annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3553"}]}],"name":"DeepCell","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41592-020-01023-0","metadata":{"abstract":"Deep learning is transforming the analysis of biological images, but applying these models to large datasets remains challenging. Here we describe the DeepCell Kiosk, cloud-native software that dynamically scales deep learning workflows to accommodate large imaging datasets. To demonstrate the scalability and affordability of this software, we identified cell nuclei in 106 1-megapixel images in ~5.5 h for ~US$250, with a cost below US$100 achievable depending on cluster configuration. The DeepCell Kiosk can be downloaded at https://github.com/vanvalenlab/kiosk-console; a persistent deployment is available at https://deepcell.org/.","authors":[{"name":"Bannon D."},{"name":"Borba E."},{"name":"Chang B."},{"name":"Graf W."},{"name":"Greenwald N."},{"name":"Kudo T."},{"name":"Moen E."},{"name":"Osterman E."},{"name":"Pao E."},{"name":"Schwartz M."},{"name":"Van Valen D."},{"name":"Vijayakumar V."}],"citationCount":82,"date":"2021-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"DeepCell Kiosk: scaling deep learning\u2013enabled cellular image analysis with Kubernetes"},"pmcid":"PMC8759612","pmid":"33398191","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1101/803205","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Protein expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0108"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DeepCell","home":"https://bio.tools/deepcell","summary":"Accurate cell tracking and lineage construction in live-cell imaging experiments with deep learning.\n\nHome \u2014 DeepCell 1.0.0 documentation.\n\nFree document hosting provided by Read the Docs","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:deepcell/web/www.deepcell.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"faq":true,"general":true,"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":88,"citations":[{"count":9,"year":"2021"},{"count":10,"year":"2026"},{"count":13,"year":"2022"},{"count":18,"year":"2024"},{"count":18,"year":"2025"},{"count":20,"year":"2023"}],"doi":"10.1038/s41592-020-01023-0","pmcid":"PMC8759612","pmid":"33398191","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"DeepCell Kiosk: scaling deep learning-enabled cellular image analysis with Kubernetes.","year":2021}]},{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1101/803205","ref_count":0,"refs":[]}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":308,"url":"https://www.deepcell.org/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/deepcell","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":308,"url":"https://www.deepcell.org/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>DeepCell is neural network library for single cell analysis, written in Python and built using <a href=\"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow\">TensorFlow</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/keras-team/keras\">Keras</a>.</p>\n\n<p>DeepCell aids in biological analysis by automatically segmenting and classifying cells in optical microscopy images. This framework consumes raw images and provides uniquely annotated files as an output.</p>\n\n<p>The jupyter session in the read docs are broken, but the one from the GitHub are functional (see usage example )</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>DeepCell is neural network library for single cell analysis, written in Python and built using <a href=\"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow\">TensorFlow</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/keras-team/keras\">Keras</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>DeepCell aids in biological analysis by automatically segmenting and classifying cells in optical microscopy images. This framework consumes raw images and provides uniquely annotated files as an output.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The jupyter session in the read docs are broken, but the one from the GitHub are functional (see usage example )</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2020-10-19T15:09:45+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2019-08-26T10:09:13+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[{"format":"basic_html","pr